# Lead Protocol - merge attributes for the append-only shared logs.
#
# JOURNAL.md, LESSONS.md and decisions.jsonl are append-at-tail by protocol
# rule (PROTOCOL_RULES.md §P3). Git's built-in union driver combines
# conflicting lines without adding conflict markers to those hunks.
# Ordering is arbitrary. Same-heading Markdown entries can collapse their
# boundaries and byte-identical JSONL lines can deduplicate. Distinguishable
# headings reduce collisions; union provides no locking or lossless guarantee.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed here:
#   - sessions/active_sessions.md: rows are REMOVED on session close, and a
#     union merge would silently resurrect removed rows (closed sessions
#     would reappear as live). Conflicts there must be resolved by hand.
#   - local/**: per-pair state is gitignored and never merged.
#
# See modules/git-substrate.md §M-git-8 for the full merge contract.

JOURNAL.md merge=union
LESSONS.md merge=union
decisions.jsonl merge=union
